<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Software Engineering Notes</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f4f7fb;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 15px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #34495e;
        }

        .topic {
            padding: 18px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            background: #edf2f7;
            border-left: 5px solid #34495e;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #34495e;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>💻 Software Engineering Notes</h1>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>What is Software Engineering?</h2>
        <p>Software engineering is the systematic approach used to develop, test and maintain software.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Software Process</h2>
        <p>A software process describes the activities followed during software development.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Requirements</h2>
        <p>Requirements describe what the software should do and what users expect from it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Design</h2>
        <p>Design describes how the software will be structured and how its components will work together.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Testing</h2>
        <p>Testing is performed to find errors and check whether the software works as expected.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="topic">
        <h2>Maintenance</h2>
        <p>Maintenance involves updating and improving software after it is delivered.</p>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
